  "summary_en": "Malaysian Civil Aviation Directive issued under the Civil Aviation Act 1969 setting requirements for approving Remote Pilot Training Organisations for drones: certificate of approval, personnel, safety management, audits, training syllabi, examinations and certification. Supports the operation-centric, risk-based UAS regime (Open, Specific, Certified).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No one may train or examine for a Remote Pilot Certificate of Competency without a valid CAAM RPTO certificate of approval, valid 12 months.",
   "RPTOs must operate a safety management system, emergency response plan and report occurrences within 48 hours.",
   "Annual CAAM oversight audits with a five-point corrective action closure plan.",
   "Defines A2 RCoC and RCoC-B competency certificates tied to Open and Specific categories; minimum ages 16 and 18.",
   "RPTOs must hold third-party liability insurance; offences are punishable under Civil Aviation Act s.24O."
  ],
